@startuml CryptoWeb-state-09-refresh-token
title CryptoWeb - Refresh Token Lifecycle

!theme plain
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype polyline
skinparam nodesep 65
skinparam ranksep 65
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam StateFontSize 14
skinparam ArrowFontSize 12
hide empty description

state "ACTIVE" as Active
state "REVOKED" as Revoked
state "EXPIRED" as Expired

[*] --> Active : login or token rotation
Active --> Revoked : refresh-token rotation or logout
Active --> Expired : expires_at reached

note right of Active
  ACTIVE means revoked is false
  and expires_at is in the future.
  The token is stored as a hash.
end note

note right of Revoked
  Refresh/logout revokes existing
  active refresh tokens for the user.
  Existing tokens cannot be reused.
end note

note right of Expired
  EXPIRED is derived from expires_at,
  not a stored ENUM value. No state
  change is necessary for expiry.
end note

@enduml
